    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44871" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπροσ-ήγορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy of address</i>, i.e.
				<i>affable, courteous</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν -οισίν
				ἐστί τις χάρις</span>; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				95
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. φρήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					775
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
					552
				</span></i>
			, cf. Trag. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gött.Nachr.</u>
				1922.31
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ λόγῳ εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				1.20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὐ. ἆται</span> miseries
			that forbid <i>my being spoken to</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				1284
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ώτατος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				19.1.13
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				5.4
			</span></i>.</div>
